from stage7_support import *
def read(n):return json.loads((OUT/(n+'.json')).read_text())
def doc(n,s):(ROOT/'docs'/('stage7_'+n+'.md')).write_text(s)
a=read('acceptance');m=read('stage7_3/memory');b=m['stm32_budget'];total=sum(v['tests'] for v in a['ctest_counts'].values())
rows='\n'.join('| '+k+' | '+str(v['rom_sections_bytes'])+' | '+str(v['ram_span_bytes'])+' |' for k,v in m['profiles'].items())
doc('memory','# Memory measurements\n\n| Profile | ROM bytes | RAM span bytes |\n|---|---:|---:|\n'+rows+'\n\nReduction: '+str(m['reduction'])+'. Baseline: 131072-byte kernel heap, 16384-byte main stack. Optimized: 4096-byte kernel heap, 6144-byte main stack, fixed 8192-byte Newlib arena through official CUSTOM_SBRK. Startup executes an overflow-rejection check. Assertions and stack painting remain enabled. Shared client archives and pools remain unchanged. QEMU memory is unchanged.\n\nRuntime watermarks: `'+json.dumps(m['runtime'])+'`. Arena peak is exact; live allocation is sampled. Input-section group totals exclude padding. Application and UART share an object. MAP/ELF, sections, pool/stack symbols, stripped ELF size comparison and hashes are referenced in memory.json. Stripping debug symbols changes file size, not runtime RAM/ROM. Test diagnostics remain in the qualified build; no untested removal savings are claimed.\n')
doc('stm32_feasibility','# STM32F103ZET6 capacity\n\nTarget Cortex-M3, Flash 512 KiB, SRAM 64 KiB: [official ST documentation](https://www.st.com/en/microcontrollers-microprocessors/stm32f103ze.html).\n\nOptimized constrained resource link: **'+b['result']+'**. Actual per-profile links: `'+json.dumps(b['profiles'])+'`. Separate MEMORY scripts constrain 512/64 KiB and include stacks, pools and the fixed Newlib arena. Baseline is NOT FIT. AN385 startup and peripheral addresses remain; this is not an STM32 BSP. Hardware: NOT TESTED.\n\nRemaining SRAM is small for BSP, DMA, SD/FatFs and further tasks. At least 128 KiB SRAM would give expansion room, a budget inference rather than a tested port. Application minimum is three publishers and one subscriber. Current fixed RMW pools reserve four publishers plus unused service/client slots; reducing these requires another full regression.\n')
rows=[]
for prefix in ['', 'optimized_']:
 for c in read('stage7_2/'+prefix+'faults')['cases']:rows.append('| '+(prefix or 'baseline_')+c['scenario']+' | '+c['status']+' | '+str(c['host_received_records'])+' | '+c['external_logs']+' |')
doc('fault_matrix','# Fault matrix\n\n| Profile/scenario | Result | Received | Logs |\n|---|---|---:|---|\n'+'\n'.join(rows)+'\n\nRecovery gate also covers delayed Agent startup, three restarts with the same QEMU PID and bounded no-Agent stopping. Real relay loss, Subscriber/MCU SIGSTOP, duplicates, invalid parameters, software reboot and partial entity creation interruption are exercised. Normal/fault GDB logs verify session lifecycle, Executor and Publisher. After detach, ACK and 256 records verify subscriptions and publication. process_exits.json records managed process exit codes. Fault-period sampled/published/forwarded/received differences remain visible in evidence.\n')
items=['Automatic Reconnect','Agent Restart Recovery','MCU Session Recovery','Command Idempotency','Long-run Data Integrity','Fault Injection','Memory Leak / Resource Stability','QEMU / GDB','Memory Optimization','Stage 0–6 Regression']
ok=a['status'].startswith('Stage 7 SOFTWARE PASS')
doc('report','# Stage 7 report\n\n'+a['status']+'\n\n| Item | Result |\n|---|---|\n'+'\n'.join('| '+i+' | '+('PASS' if ok else 'FAIL')+' |' for i in items)+'\n| STM32 Resource Fit | '+b['result']+' (optimized capacity only) |\n| Hardware | NOT TESTED |\n\nActual JUnit count: '+str(total)+' including historical '+str(read('regression/summary')['historical_total'])+'. Each stress profile validates 10000 actual MCU/Agent/Host records with zero duplicates or missing data. Finite accelerated simulation is not multi-day endurance or real MCU performance.\n\nReproduce: /usr/bin/python3 scripts/accept_stage7.py as the current user. acceptance.json records commands and exits; log_manifest.json hashes raw logs. Historical evidence is redirected during reruns and unchanged.\n\nDevelopment failures retained in raw logs: concurrent configuration invalidated generated interrupt data; sequential pristine rebuild resolved it. A retained allocator pointer required static lifetime. Short active probes caused a false reconnect under pressure; bounded longer probes replaced them. Failed runs do not count as passed acceptance.\n\nStage 8 not implemented.\n')
print('DOCUMENTS_WRITTEN',total)
